# Erdős Problem #99 — repository campaign review and handoff

**Date:** 2026-09-09

**Reviewed state before this report:** `d9f8f3c`, then remote coordination through `ca31415`
**Run type:** synthesis, regression audit, reproducibility repair

**Target:** A / B / C / repository state

**External search:** no new search in this review; previously imported sources were rechecked by their cited reports

**Computation:** exact repository tests and listed research scripts

## LEVEL I STATUS

**STILL OPEN.** No branch has been promoted to a proof or disproof of Erdős
Problem #99. The original quantifier remains: every sufficiently large global
minimum-diameter unit-separated configuration must contain a unit equilateral
triangle, or there must be infinitely many globally optimal triangle-free
cardinalities. Neither direction is closed.

This review is a state correction and handoff. It does not silently promote a
higher-numbered report over the route maps, and it does not treat numerical or
local evidence as global optimality.

The subsequent [zero-transfer and defect-train review](campaign_zero_transfer_defect_review_2026-09-09.md)
records the complete Z–DF dependency audit, the exact pentagon competitor, the
SEPq sign-convention correction, and verification after the coordinated merge.
Its conditional exceptional-face conclusion does not close the global problem.

